<div type="translation" resp="part:emfr">
      		
   <div type="textpart" subtype="item" n="A">
      <head xml:lang="eng">South Pillar</head>
      <p n="1">
         He who is a hook for pain / He whose hook is painful.<note>See other <foreign>biruda</foreign>s of the Pallavas ending in <foreign>aṅkuśa</foreign>, e.g., in inscription <ref target="DHARMA_INSPallava00055">Pallava 55</ref>.</note>
      </p>
   </div>
   
   <div type="textpart" subtype="item" n="B">
      <head xml:lang="eng">North Pillar</head>
      <p n="1">
         He who is an able Pṛthu.<note>Pṛthu is a mythical paragon of kingship.</note>
      </p>
   </div>
</div>
      	
